  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Dobbm. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Dobbm is a traditional trick-taking game unique to the Stubai Valley in Tyrol, Austria. It is an 'Ace-Ten' game related to Tarock and Tapp, played with a 36-card Tell-pattern deck. The name refers to the 4-card talon known as the 'Dobb'.",
    objective: 'Win tricks to capture point cards and reach a target score. Points are: Ace/Sow (11), Ten (10), King (4), Ober (3), Unter (2). Total: 120 points per hand.',
    gameplay: "1. Bidding: Players bid 'Ordinary' or 'Solo'. In an Ordinary game, the declarer takes the 'Dobb' and discards 4 cards (points count for them).\n2. Trumps: Declarer names the trump suit.\n3. The Dobb: In a Solo, the Dobb points count for the dealer (who is celebrating), not the soloist.\n4. Card Play: Clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, must play a trump if possible.",
    keyRules: [
      "The 6 of Bells ('Weli') is just a normal card in Dobbm.",
      "The Ace is called the 'Sow' (Sau).",
      "Defenders can 'schieben' (smear) points on their partner's trick.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: "4 active players. If 5 play, the dealer 'feiert' (takes a holiday) and sits out.",
      deck: '36 German-suited (Tell) cards. Suits: Hearts, Leaves, Acorns, Bells.',
      equipment: '36-card deck, score sheet.',
      dealing: "8 cards to each player dealt in batches of 4. Four cards go face-down to the center as the 'Dobb'. The dealer for a hand is always the 'declarer' from the previous hand.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Bidding: Players bid 'Ordinary' or 'Solo'. In an Ordinary game, the declarer takes the 'Dobb' and discards 4 cards (points count for them).\n2. Trumps: Declarer names the trump suit.\n3. The Dobb: In a Solo, the Dobb points count for the dealer (who is celebrating), not the soloist.\n4. Card Play: Clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, must play a trump if possible.",
